Project Development Phase
PocketSmart AI: Your Smart Budget & Recommendation Assistant

Project Development Phase

1. Introduction

The Development Phase is the stage where the PocketSmart AI design and requirements are converted into a working application. During this phase, the frontend, backend, database, budget calculation, and AI recommendation features are developed and integrated.

2. Development Objectives

The main objectives are:

To create a simple and user-friendly budgeting application.

To allow users to enter their income and expenses.

To automatically calculate the remaining budget.

To categorize and track expenses.

To provide personalized recommendations using AI.

To display financial information clearly using charts and summaries.


3. Technology Stack

Component	Technology

Frontend	HTML, CSS, JavaScript
Backend	Python / Flask
Database	SQLite
AI	Google Gemini API
Charts	Chart.js
Development Tool	Visual Studio Code
Version Control	Git & GitHub


4. Frontend Development

The frontend is developed to provide an easy interface for users.

Main screens/features:

Home/Dashboard

Income entry

Expense entry

Expense categories

Budget summary

AI recommendation section

Charts and reports


The interface uses HTML for structure, CSS for styling, and JavaScript for interactive features.

5. Backend Development

The backend handles the application's main operations.

It performs:

User input processing

Income and expense calculations

Budget calculations

Data storage and retrieval

Communication with the AI service

Sending results back to the frontend


6. Database Development

An SQLite database is used to store financial information.

Example tables:

Income Table

Income ID

Amount

Source

Date


Expense Table

Expense ID

Category

Amount

Description

Date


Budget Table

Budget ID

Category

Budget Amount

Period


7. Budget Calculation Module

The system calculates the available budget automatically.

Formula:

Remaining Budget = Total Income − Total Expenses

It can also calculate category-wise spending and compare actual expenses with the planned budget.

8. AI Recommendation Module

The AI module analyzes the user's budget information and generates personalized suggestions.

For example, based on spending data, it can provide recommendations such as:

Reduce unnecessary expenses.

Set a monthly spending limit.

Allocate more money toward savings.

Monitor categories with high spending.


The Gemini API can be integrated into the backend to generate these recommendations.

9. Expense Tracking

Users can enter expenses with details such as:

Amount

Category

Description

Date


Expenses can be grouped into categories such as:

Food

Transport

Education

Shopping

Entertainment

Bills

Others


10. Dashboard Development

The dashboard provides a quick overview of the user's financial status.

It displays:

Total income

Total expenses

Remaining balance

Category-wise expenses

Budget status

AI-generated recommendations


Charts can be used to make the information easier to understand.

11. Integration

After developing individual modules, they are integrated into one application.

The integration connects:

User → Frontend → Backend → Database → AI Module → Recommendation → Frontend

This allows the user to enter financial information and receive calculations and recommendations within the same application.

12. Testing During Development

Each module is tested while development is in progress.

Examples:

Checking whether income is stored correctly.

Checking expense calculations.

Testing category-wise totals.

Testing database operations.

Checking AI recommendation responses.

Testing frontend and backend communication.


13. Development Outcome

At the end of the Development Phase, PocketSmart AI becomes a functional budgeting application that can record income and expenses, calculate budgets, visualize spending, and provide AI-based personalized recommendations.

14. Conclusion

The Development Phase transforms the PocketSmart AI concept and design into a working software system. By integrating the frontend, backend, database, and AI recommendation module, the project provides users with a convenient way to track expenses, manage budgets, understand spending patterns, and receive personalized financial suggestions.
